+means no added whitespace at all**, which is the only setting that cannot
+change what the page means: whitespace between inline elements is text the
+browser renders. Indenting is for reading the output while developing, and
+even then the content of `pre`, `textarea`, `script` and `style` is left
+exactly as written, as is an element whose only child is text.
